{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"Review of issue #605 found that ACP Timeline creation opened a Session and journaled its transition before NodeRegistry committed Timeline genesis; a crash in that interval left no reconstructable Timeline.","decision":"Make ACP Timeline creation establish only the Gnostic Timeline projection. Open and journal the ACP Session on the first Turn, after the Timeline genesis event has been committed.","impact":"ACP Session creation is deferred from Timeline create to first Turn. Journal projections remain the authority for Gnostic identity even when the ACP Runtime no longer lists a Session. No dependency or storage-format change was added.","recurrence_control":"Added NodeRuntime tests for genesis-before-Session ordering and Timeline recovery after removing ACP fixture Sessions. make verify, make container-smoke, make runner-smoke, make acp-smoke, and git diff --check passed.","rejected_alternatives":["Write Timeline genesis from the ACP backend before remote creation; failed remote creation could leave a durable Timeline that was never accepted by Gnostic."],"sources":[]}
